  "notes": "The main hall of the Kagami Pond temple, 14 m by 11 m and 9.5 m to the ridge: a 1 m basalt plinth with wooden steps, a 1 m veranda on all four sides, a slate irimoya roof with lifted corners, an open front and sides under a lattice band, and paper screens on the back wall. Faces local -Z (the pond); the open front leads to an altar and stone light at the back.",
